From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:47:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): placed kanban_create returns the hub task id
 (bounded outcome fetch), says a queued card IS created, never resends an
 identical retry [daveey]

A chat that got task_id null from a hub-placed kanban_create read it as not created and called
kanban_create again, creating a stray card (10-27 drill). The request result only reached the
MacBook on a later full hermes-hub sync (~30 s), so the 8 s poll of the local replica never saw it.

- await_task_id: hermes-hub outcomes (client 1.9.1+) about once a second, else ONE detached sync,
  for wait_seconds (default 10); the task id and hub status come back top-level.
- Still pending: status queued, note says the card IS created and a second call duplicates it.
- An identical retry (same stable request id) is not sent again and is flagged retry.
- remote_task_id also reads a plain create's truncated output text.
---
